{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom/fold.go at exact 9c663be7b3e031880df8e5f3e9998214ee6f4f19 on request/succession-append-cost, under promise git:sha1…ecd1ad1 on request git:sha1…5f12606\n\nRequest dd845a00: cut the per-act cost of appending a merge's succession. Seven commits over main 5876d211.\n\nWhere the time went: at artroom depth, every act paid several whole-projection renders, each running the whole-log staleness pass, on the client before signing and on the resident at sequencing. Fixes:\n- dbd8947f3: the workspace renders its projection only when a reader first asks, and admission reuses its own rendering while the head has not moved.\n- ffbad96de: the kind-defined status check runs only for a replayed act. Admission already refuses an undefined kind at the head the act joins.\n- 64caff2a4 and 9c663be7b: each receipt's successor paths are decoded once, and its narrowed plan is computed once per staleness pass.\n- 69dd75ac5: admission keeps the events a refusal advanced over. This fixes a defect that predates the lane, which the review found.\n- afaf96dfa: a snapshot read is timed together with the render it pays for.\n- 7b4e3f5af: comments only.\n\nConditions:\n1. Measured with instrumented binaries on the frozen artroom copy, load 8.8–10, main → head: successor artifact 3.48 s → 0.63 s; retirement 1.12 s → 0.12 s; merge receipt 59.3 s → 22.3 s. The instrumented binaries skipped the per-label PriorAct preflight scan on both sides; request bb5f2acd removes that scan. Before the change, the resident spent 193 of 220 s on renders, mostly the staleness pass.\n2. The 162-act succession took 318.1 s before and 49.2 s after. The independent reviewer, using the unmodified head binary, measured 48 s (0.30 s per act).\n3. Every act is still built and signed by the client, submitted on its own, admitted by the post-dedup hook, sequencer-signed, and appended by compare-and-swap.\n4. Cold projections are byte-identical between main and the head at depths 43,744, 43,907 and the post-succession frontier.\n5. go test ./... -count=1 passes at 9c663be7; go test -race on internal/app and cmd/gs passes; go vet is clean.\n\nMemory: admission now keeps a second full projection for the life of the resident (about 71 MB as JSON at depth 43,907). Peak resident RSS with no readers was 1,280 MB at the head against 1,761 MB on main. With a reader polling after every act, each poll still renders, and the next act waits for that render.\n\nTests that pin the work: TestSequencedActsRenderTheSnapshotOnlyWhenRead, TestAdmissionRendersItsWorldOncePerHead, TestOnlyAReplayAsksWhetherItsKindIsDefined, TestTwoMergesEachLendOnlyTheirOwnPlan, TestAnEmptyPathDoesNotBorrowTheMergePlan, TestAdmissionWorldKeepsTheEventsARefusalAdvancedOver (red on main) and TestADeferredRenderIsTimedByTheReadThatPaysForIt. Each goes red under its mutant.","body":{"commit":"9c663be7b3e031880df8e5f3e9998214ee6f4f19","path":"internal/workroom/fold.go"}}